# cmderr=0 when accessing data0 while busy

Hi,

as you can see from the attached waveform
![Screenshot from 2019-09-13 13-36-42](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/25659164/66300764-2d3bbf80-e8f6-11e9-9490-5413a682afdf.png)
there is an attemped data write while the previous command (another data write) was still ongoing, and there is no cmderr flagging the conflict as per specs (paragraph 3.1211)
`Accessing these registers while an abstract command is executing causes cmderr to be set to 1 (busy) if it is 0.`








PR title: return CmdErrBusy if accessing data or progbuf while command was executing

Source: https://github.com/pulp-platform/riscv-dbg/pull/79

PR description:
This PR addresses a compliance issue with the RISC-V Debug Specification (section 3.12.6). The implementation was incomplete - it only blocked writes and autoexec operations during command execution but failed to set the error flag.

Comments:
- noytzach (Author, Sep 10, 2020): According to the spec, "an abstract command was executing while command, abstractcs, or abstractauto was written, or when one of the data or progbuf registers was read or written." The current code only prevented writes but didn't return the proper error code.
- Silabs-ArjanB (Oct 15, 2020): Noted an additional specification requirement: "This status is only written if cmderr contains 0." Suggested modifying the implementation to only set CmdErrBusy when no previous error exists, preventing error overwriting.
- noytzach (Oct 27, 2020): Accepted the suggestion and implemented the correction in commit 0a54bd7.
- bluewww (Nov 6, 2020): Approved the changes with "lgtm, thanks for the patch" and merged the PR.

Linked issue:
- Closes #37 "cmderr=0 when accessing data0 while busy"

Status: Merged on Nov 6, 2020.
